  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nIn the context of digital wallets, the [OpenID for Verifiable Presentations (OID4VP) 1.0](https://openid.net/specs/openid-4-verifiable-presentations-1_0.html) specification defines a new URI scheme, [openid4vp:](https://openid.net/specs/openid-4-verifiable-presentations-1_0.html#name-openid4vp).\n\nThe openid4vp: scheme is the prevailing method used by OID4VP verifiers to invoke a wallet, but it currently only works with non-web (native) wallets.\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\n_No response_\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nTo enable web/PWA wallets to interoperate with web clients (OID4VP verifiers) that use the openid4vp: invocation method, those wallets must be able to register a protocol handler, either with navigator.registerProtocolHandler() or via the Web App Manifest (for PWAs).\n\nThis requires the openid4vp: scheme to be safelisted by browsers.\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
